   "reply_to_post_number": null,
   "like_count": 2,
   "cooked": "<p>Love it!</p>\n<p>We should check on a couple things…</p>\n<p><span class=\"hashtag\">#1</span> We will eventually move to our own discord</p>\n<p><span class=\"hashtag\">#2</span> How easy is it to add new repos to the party</p>\n<p><span class=\"hashtag\">#3</span> We might want to have 2 channels, one for all the github activity, and another for Project Management, as we are using this repo to organize work in general: <a href=\"https://github.com/TECommons/Coordination\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">https://github.com/TECommons/Coordination</a>…</p>",
   "action": null,
   "source": {
    "source": "commoncrawl",
    "timestamp": "20260121133036",
    "url": "https://forum.tecommons.org/t/have-a-github-activity-channel-on-discord/60"
   }
  },
  {
